# Secrets
.env

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Data. Raw and processed parquet are committed on purpose, about 28 MB, so the
# Power BI model and the analysis open on another machine without an API key or
# a 15-minute re-pull. The DuckDB warehouse stays out: 58 MB, and it rebuilds
# from the parquet in seconds.
data/interim/*
# CSV copies are a 86 MB on-demand fallback (make csv); parquet is the committed form.
data/processed/*.csv
!data/interim/.gitkeep

# Power BI. The project files under powerbi/grid_stress.SemanticModel and
# powerbi/grid_stress.Report are the source: they are text, they diff, and
# Power BI Desktop opens grid_stress.pbip directly. A .pbix is a build output
# that embeds its own copy of the data, so it is not committed.
*.pbix
*.pbix.bak
powerbi/.pbi/
powerbi/**/.pbi/localSettings.json
powerbi/**/*.abf

# Ad-hoc SQL scratchpad
scratch/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
